  "necessity_paragraph": "The patient presents with intermittent palpitations and a sensation of irregular heartbeat, which are concerning for potential arrhythmias in the context of known nonrheumatic mitral valve insufficiency (I34.0, R00.2). Mobile cardiac telemetry (CPT 93229) is ordered to capture continuous rhythm data during daily activities to correlate these symptoms with any underlying cardiac conduction abnormalities. Because the required precertification was not obtained before services were rendered, the payer denied the claim under Reason Code CO-197, and this appeal requests that the missing prior authorization be reviewed against the documented clinical indication."
